# Class: obo:SWO_1000058 (Purchase cost)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1000058 "Purchase cost is a license clause which states whether there is a cost involved with a particular usage or licensing of a resource.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_1000058 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:SWO_1000058 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:SWO_1000058 "In some ways, purchase cost is similar to the already-extant usage clause hierarchy, which includes restricted and unrestricted usage. However, a usage limitation is not necessarily due to whether or not something costs money: even if the usage is academic only, it could still be either free or non-free. A license could have multiple usage clauses, e.g. academic only when free, and unrestricted if a fee is paid. Purchase cost was created which, together with a usage clause, defines both limitations and cost.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_1000058 "Purchase cost")
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_1000058 obo:SWO_9000005)

# Class: obo:SWO_1000059 (Free)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1000059 "Free is a type of purchase cost clause which, when applied, means that there is no cost for the users of the resource to which the license is attached. This clause can be combined with other clauses (such as usage clauses) to specify that only certain usages are free.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_1000059 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_1000059 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:SWO_1000059 "This class refers only to the cost of the resource, not to the definition of \"free software\" as provided by the GNU Project and which is commonly used to describe software that respects users' freedom and community (http://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.html).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_1000059 "Free")
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_1000059 obo:SWO_1000058)

# Class: obo:SWO_1000060 (Not Free)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1000060 "Not Free is a type of purchase cost clause which, when applied, means that there is a cost for the users of the resource to which the license is attached. This clause can be combined with other clauses (such as usage clauses) to specify that only certain usages incur a purchase cost.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_1000060 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_1000060 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:SWO_1000060 "This class refers only to the cost of the resource, not to the definition of \"free software\" as provided by the GNU Project and which is commonly used to describe software that respects users' freedom and community (http://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.html).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_1000060 "Not Free")
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_1000060 obo:SWO_1000058)

# Class: obo:SWO_1000061 (free to use license)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1000061 "A license which allows any form of usage of the artifact.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_1000061 "free to use license"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_1000061 obo:SWO_0000002)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_1000061 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:SWO_9001002 obo:SWO_9000030))

# Class: obo:SWO_1000065 (CC BY 4.0)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1000065 "The CC BY 4.0 license is a Creative Commons license. This is a non-copyleft free license that is good for art and entertainment works, and educational works. It is compatible with all versions of the GNU GPL; however, like all CC licenses, it should not be used on software. People are free to:
Share — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format;
Adapt — remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose, even commercially.
The licensor cannot revoke these freedoms as long as you follow the license terms.
But they must conform to the following terms:
Attribution — You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the license, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in any way that suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.
No additional restrictions — You may not apply legal terms or technological measures that legally restrict others from doing anything the license permits.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:SWO_1000065 "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_1000065 "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ accessed June 22, 2016; https://www.gnu.org/licenses/license-list.html, accessed on June 28, 2016.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_1000065 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:SWO_1000065 "Allyson Lister: The only restriction on derivatives is that of the attribution requirement. ")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_1000065 "CC BY 4.0"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_1000065 obo:SWO_1000001)
