# Class: obo:SWO_3000070 (tabix file format)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_3000070 "Tabix indexes a TAB-delimited genome position file and creates an index file when region is absent from the command-line. The input data file must be position sorted and compressed by bgzip which has a gzip like interface. After indexing, tabix is able to quickly retrieve data lines overlapping regions specified in the format \"chr:beginPos-endPos\". Fast data retrieval also works over network if URI is given as a file name and in this case the index file will be downloaded if it is not present locally.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000070 "http://samtools.sourceforge.net/tabix.shtml")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_3000070 "tabix file format")
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_3000070 obo:SWO_3000069)

# Class: obo:SWO_3000071 (genomedata format)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_3000071 "Genomedata provides a way to store and access large-scale functional genomics data in a format which is both space-efficient and allows efficient random-access. Genomedata archives are implemented as one or more HDF5 files, either as single files or as directory archives. HDF5 archives are self describing, like XML, but may also contain more complex structures such contain binary data.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000071 "http://pmgenomics.ca/hoffmanlab/proj/genomedata/doc/1.3.5/genomedata.html and http://www.hdfgroup.org/why_hdf/, accessed 27 November 2014.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_3000071 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_3000071 "genomedata format"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_3000071 obo:IAO_0000098)

# Class: obo:SWO_3000072 (BedGraph)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_3000072 "The bedGraph format is a line-oriented text file format. Bedgraph data are preceeded by a track definition line, which adds a number of options for controlling the default display of this track. Following the track definition line are the track data in four column BED format. The bedGraph format allows display of continuous-valued data in track format. This display type is useful for probability scores and transcriptome data. This track type is similar to the wiggle (WIG) format, but unlike the wiggle format, data exported in the bedGraph format are preserved in their original state.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000072 "http://genome.ucsc.edu/goldenpath/help/bedgraph.html, accessed December 3, 2014.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_3000072 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_3000072 "BedGraph"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_3000072 <http://edamontology.org/format_2330>)

# Class: obo:SWO_3000073 (GMTK parameter data)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_3000073 "GMTK parameter data is a type of data which contains the various parameter files required by GMTK to define a dynamic Bayesian network.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:SWO_3000073 "Graphical Models Toolkit parameter data")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000073 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000073 "http://noble.gs.washington.edu/proj/philius/README, accessed 3 December 2014.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_3000073 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_3000073 "GMTK parameter data"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_3000073 obo:IAO_0000027)

# Class: obo:SWO_3000074 (MathML 2.0)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_3000074 "MathML 2.0 is an XML format which is a low-level specification for describing mathematics as a basis for machine to machine communication. It is a W3C Recommendation and was released on 21 Feb 2001. A product of the W3C Math working group, it provides a much needed foundation for the inclusion of mathematical expressions in Web pages.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000074 "http://www.w3.org/Math/")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_3000074 "Allyson Lister")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_3000074 "James Malone")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_3000074 "MathML 2.0")
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_3000074 <http://edamontology.org/format_2332>)

# Class: obo:SWO_3000075 (FieldML)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_3000075 "FieldML is an XML-based language for describing time-varying and
spatially-varying fields. The aims of the language design process are to
keep the language concise, consistent, intuitive and flexible.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:SWO_3000075 "http://www.physiomeproject.org/xml_languages/fieldml")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:creator obo:SWO_3000075 "James Malone")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_3000075 "FieldML"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:SWO_3000075 <http://edamontology.org/format_2332>)

# Class: obo:SWO_3000076 (WKn)

